{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"agent_message","text":"The exploration reached a real slow-path Accept. The owner counted the recipient’s reply, but the recipient remained `PREACCEPTED` and reported that phase in a later Prepare response. Its sequence, dependencies, and value ballot were retained. Recovery uses status separately from those fields, so I’ll define a local phase-retention obligation without claiming that a decided value was lost.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));c=[x for x in r['candidates'] if x['id']=='034d70569cf0415abd1f6d31beae20f7'][0];q=c['question'];q['disposition']='ready_for_check';q['unknowns']=['A full recovery decision conflict is independent of the local accepted-phase reporting obligation.'];q['trigger_rationale']='Producer-backed exploration 563eae5f1d964500bd0c94f432fbf06a reached slow-path Accept via differing real PreAccept replies, counted its acknowledgment, and observed recipient and subsequent Prepare status remain PREACCEPTED. Retained attributes/vbal do not encode phase: PreAccept already sets those fields, and recovery independently branches on Status.'\nclaim=dict(id='C-accept-phase',kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='After acknowledging a nonstale Accept for a preaccepted instance, the recipient must retain the accepted phase and report ACCEPTED in a subsequent Prepare response when no intervening value-changing or commit operation has occurred.',source_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery'],scope=dict(description='Live recipient acceptance-phase accounting and Prepare reporting between a successful Accept acknowledgment and the next higher-ballot Prepare, without intervening commit or value change.',assumptions=['Fixed membership and non-Byzantine complete request/reply delivery.','Instance commands were established by actual PreAccept; matching-ballot Accept is generated by its coordinator slow path.','Only Prepare follows Accept at the recipient in the measured interval.'],excluded=['No quorum decision loss, cluster agreement violation, execution outcome or client completion claim.','No durable restart or automatic recovery-trigger guarantee.','Independent VBallot codec loss and self-reply relabeling are not the status oracle.']),pending=[],grounding=dict(source_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery'],expectation_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery'],binding_ids=['BD-accept-phase','BD-prepare-status'],derivation='The composed local contract follows from actual consumers: handleAcceptReply counts a matching-ballot AcceptReply toward an ACCEPTED coordinator decision; handlePrepare reports the recipient phase; handlePrepareReply explicitly distinguishes ACCEPTED (continue Accept) from preaccepted states (which may restart phase one). Thus the acknowledgment must be backed by retained acceptance phase, even before a decision quorum. The obligation is not that a preaccepted command must be chosen. Retaining vbal/seq/deps is insufficient to represent phase because PreAccept also sets vbal to the same ballot and recovery reads Status independently. In the stated interval Prepare may raise joined bal but does not constitute a new value acceptance or invalidate prior accepted phase.',applicability='Nonstale Accept on command-bearing preaccepted state, followed only by higher-ballot Prepare. Excludes already committed recipients and stale requests; exact ACCEPTED applies because no later commit/execution has occurred.',unresolved=[],conflicts=[],alternatives=['Commit would establish a later phase but is absent during the scoped interval.','Attributes and ballots are retained, which limits the defect to phase accounting rather than total value loss.']))\nbind=[]\nfor id,mat,sym,a,b in [('BD-accept-phase','S-formation','Replica.handleAccept',974,1006),('BD-prepare-status','S-recovery','Replica.handlePrepare',1171,1202)]:\n bind.append(dict(id=id,material_id=mat,symbol=sym,start_line=a,end_line=b,description='Recipient acceptance and subsequent prior-state reporting boundary.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim['id'],source_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery'],rationale='Acknowledged acceptance must be represented in the phase that the later recovery consumer distinguishes.')]))\nm=json.load(open('../audit-spec/v2.json'))\nfor b in m['behaviors']:\n if b['id']=='B-formation':\n  b['unknowns'][0]='Whether the retained preaccepted status after acknowledgment can lead to a different decision in a complete recovery history remains open.'\n  b['existing_protections']=['Accept retains seq/deps and bal/vbal, but these are also set by PreAccept and do not independently identify accepted phase.','Smaller-ballot Accept and already-committed state have guards.']\njson.dump(m,open('map-accept.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=c['id'],question=q,obligation=claim,bindings=bind,map_path='map-accept.json',map_changes={'B-formation':dict(impact='clarification',source_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery'],rationale='Clarify the already-observed absence of recipient Status assignment and its distinct consumer role; preserve separate decision-history uncertainty.',preserves='F-state remains local reported phase, not proof of quorum support; no change to identity, producer/consumer edges or prior codec obligation.')},rationale='Ground local accepted-phase retention from the acknowledgment and recovery interface, based on an executed producer history without inferring a decision violation.',feedback=dict(ref_ids=[c['id'],'B-formation','B-authority','563eae5f1d964500bd0c94f432fbf06a','S-formation','S-recovery'],answered='Exploration generated differing PreAccept replies in a five-node configuration, causing owner 1 to emit Accept for instance 1.0 at ballot 1. Recipient 2 acknowledged it and the owner counted one acceptOK. Recipient status remained PREACCEPTED (1), with vbal 1 and seq 1 retained. A generated Prepare ballot 5 then returned status 1, matching live state, while preserving the dependency vector and command count. No Accept quorum or Commit was delivered. Source distinguishes phase from vbal/attributes, so retained fields do not supply equivalent accepted-phase information.',remaining=['A fresh fixed check and correspondence review are needed for the local obligation.','Any later decision conflict remains an independent endpoint/history question.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The measured acknowledgment answers producer reachability; status in Prepare is a separate observation from the already confirmed VBallot codec mismatch.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission9.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-05_09-58-13-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission9.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
